name 'ai-and-algorithmic-decisions-postassessment-q9_2026'

question 'A weather app needs to show the forecast for any city the user types in. The developer writes `getForecast(city)` so the same function works for "Austin," "Boise," or anywhere else. What is `city` in this function?'

wrong 'A condition that must be true for the function to run.'
wrong 'A separate event handler.'
right 'A parameter — a named input that gets replaced with the actual city the user types when the function is called.'
wrong 'A loop that runs until the forecast loads.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

